---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; User Wrappable + Chainable (requires Fallible superclass)\n;\n; Tests `?` (wrap) and `Chainable:chain` on user-defined `Box[T]`.\n\ntype Box[T] = Full(T) | Empty\n\nclass Fallible for Box {\n  fun unwrap(b: Box[T]) -> T {\n    match b {\n      Box.Full(x) => { x }\n      Box.Empty => { raise \"empty box\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nclass Wrappable for Box {\n  fun wrap(x: T) -> Box[T] {\n    Box.Full(x)\n  }\n}\n\nclass Chainable for Box {\n  fun chain(b: Box[T], f: (T) -> Box[U]) -> Box[U] {\n    match b {\n      Box.Full(x) => { f(x) }\n      Box.Empty => { Box.Empty }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfun main() {\n  let b = ?42\n  let c = Chainable:chain(b, x => Box.Full(x + 1))\n  write c!\n}\n"
---
43
